For $n\geq2$, put $L=m-1+2n$. The map
\[
 (x,y)\longmapsto(u,v)=(x-y+n,x+2y+n)
\]
is a bijection from $S_m(n)$ to
\begin{equation}
 P(L,n)=\{(u,v)\in\Z^2:0\leq u,v\leq L,\quad
 n<u+v<2L-n,\quad u\equiv v\pmod3\}.
\end{equation}
Moreover $v(n)=a_2(n)$ for all $n\geq0$. Consequently
\begin{equation}
 a_5(n)=v(n)+4n+7\qquad(n\geq2).
\end{equation}
